BEGIN:VEVENT
CATEGORIES:ThoughtfulLearning
CATEGORIES:Academic/Educational
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a discussion of Predicted: How AI Is Restructuring
  Social Life\, with the book’s author\, Mona Sloane\, hosted by UVA law p
 rofessors Danielle Keats Citron and Elizabeth Rowe\, featuring sociologis
 t Jenny L. Davis\, information and public policy scholar Kirsten Martin\,
  and law professor Ari Waldman.\nWe usually talk about AI as a technology
  with social consequences\, whether for the labor force\, educational out
 comes\, or the future of humanity itself. Sloane argues it’s something el
 se: a new kind of social infrastructure\, one that installs prediction as
  an organizing principle of social life. In her new book Predicted\, she 
 shows that AI’s effects aren’t downstream of engineering decisions\, but 
 that they grow out of social practices\, institutional logics\, and profe
 ssional authority that have been technologically reified through AI.\nThr
 ough what she terms “the prediction paradigm\,” this mode of social organ
 ization forecloses debate before it starts\, settling questions about our
  shared future in places most of us never see. Predicted aims to make tho
 se arrangements visible\, putting them back up for discussion. This book 
 talk is an argument for recouping collective deliberation in the age of A
 I—about which futures with AI we want\, and what innovation is actually f
 or.\nBooks will be available for sale on site at the event.\n\nHosted by:
  Digital Technology for Democracy Lab\n\nAdditional Information can be fo
 und at: https://hoosinvolved.virginia.edu/event/12621313
DTEND:20260910T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20260902T123417Z
DTSTART:20260910T210000Z
GEO:38.053060;-78.509370
LOCATION:UVA Law School\, Purcell Reading Room
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Book Launch: An Evening About Our Future with AI
UID:https://hoosinvolved.virginia.edu/event/12621313
URL:https://hoosinvolved.virginia.edu/event/12621313
X-HOSTS:Digital Technology for Democracy Lab
END:VEVENT
