CATEGORIES:ThoughtfulLearning
CATEGORIES:Academic/Educational
DESCRIPTION:Co-Opting AI: Archives will examine how archives and archiving
 —as infrastructure\, epistemology\, and social practice—relate to contemp
 orary AI systems.\nThe Co-Opting AI series creates a public dialogue on t
 he big questions AI conjures up beyond the technology itself. It puts the
  most forward-thinking scholars across technology\, design and inequality
  into conversation with the public and covers a wide spectrum of concerns
 .\nThe series is convened by Mona Sloane\, DTD Lab faculty co-lead\, and 
 is co-hosted by NYU's Institute for Public Knowledge and Sloane Lab.\n\nH
 osted by: Digital Technology for Democracy Lab\n\nOnline Location: https:
 //dtdlab.virginia.edu/event/co-opting-ai-archives/\n\nAdditional Informat
 ion can be found at: https://hoosinvolved.virginia.edu/event/12540975
DTEND:20260923T211500Z
DTSTAMP:20260902T123417Z
DTSTART:20260923T200000Z
LOCATION:Online
